wikipedia_extract: Takao (高雄) was the lead vessel in the Takao-class heavy cruisers,
  active in World War II with the Imperial Japanese Navy. These were the largest cruisers
  in the Japanese fleet, and were intended to form the backbone of a multipurpose
  long-range strike force. Her sister ships were Atago, Maya and Chōkai. Takao was
  the only ship of her class to survive the war. She was surrendered to British forces
  at Singapore in September 1945, then sunk as a target ship in 1946.
